title: $:/plugins/crosseye/json-convert/readme

! JSON Convert

The conversion runtime: reads a JSON document, applies a //profile//
describing how each record becomes a tiddler, stages the result for
preview and collision resolution, and writes it to the wiki.

This plugin is the engine and the panels that run it.  It has no
authoring tools of its own:

* Profiles are tiddlers tagged `$:/tags/json-convert/profile`.  Custom transforms are tiddlers tagged `$:/tags/json-convert/transform` (JavaScript or wikitext bodies, `value` in scope).
* To build or edit profiles with a form, pickers and live validation, install [[JSON Convert Studio|$:/plugins/crosseye/json-convert-studio]] alongside this plugin.  The Studio adds the Console, the profile editor and the full usage guide.
* Wikitext authors can compose their own panel from the runtime's `ui/` components and the `json-convert-run` / `json-convert-apply` widgets; the Studio's Console is built from exactly these pieces.

